  "full_text": "In the days of my youth, I was told what it means to be a man. In the days of my youth, I was told what it means to be a man. I've reached that age, I try to do all those things the best I can. But no matter how I try, I find my way into the same old jam. Bad times, bad times, you know I've had my share. When a woman left home for a bad man, still don't seem to care. Sixteen, fell in love, girl as sweet as could be. It only took a couple of days before she was rid of me. Well, I swore that she would be all mine and love me till the end. But when I whispered in her ear, I lost another friend. Oh, good times.",
